What is delegate?

A delegate is a type-safe function pointer that stores references to methods and allows methods to be passed as parameters.

Delegate vs Event

Delegate                                              Event
Function reference                                    Notification mechanism
Can invoke anywhere                                   Only publisher can invoke
Used for callbacks                                    Used for publisher-subscriber


Why += in events?

Because delegates support multicast invocation list.

